    title: 'Add film grain that looks like film',
    seoTitle: 'Add film grain that looks like film, not noise',
    summary: 'Grain makes digital images feel printed and hides banding and mild softness. How much to use, why grain size matters more than amount, where to put it in the layer stack, and why it must be judged at the output size.',
    description: 'Add realistic film grain: Film Grain at Amount 10 to 25 with a small grain size, on top of the stack, judged at 100 per cent and output size. Why grain beats noise, and how it fixes banding. Live example.',
